<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.8"/>
    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Three weeks of headaches on waking, with ten days of pauses in finding words and clumsiness of the right hand, in a previously well woman of 54: an intracranial lesion must be excluded. MRI of the brain with and without contrast booked for tomorrow morning, and neuro-oncology review booked: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Late effects of childhood poliomyelitis: paralysis of the left leg in early childhood, treated with a metal brace, a special shoe, massage and heat, with full recovery of walking by about age 12 and a later career as an Olympic sprinter; no new weakness, fatigue or pain now to suggest post-polio syndrome: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Urgent neuro-oncology consultation within one week, together with neurosurgery, to review the brain MRI with her and plan diagnosis and treatment if it shows a tumor. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Central Nervous System Cancers (2026); Weller M, et al. EANO guidelines on the diagnosis and treatment of diffuse gliomas of adulthood. Nat Rev Clin Oncol 2021;18(3):170-186 (PMID 33293629) (2021) [S]</item><item>New progressive focal neurologic symptoms are imaged promptly: MRI of the brain with and without contrast within 24 hours, with same-day emergency care if she worsens, has a seizure, vomits or becomes drowsy; blood count, chemistry and A1c; no driving until the cause is known. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Central Nervous System Cancers (2026); Weller M, et al. EANO guidelines on the diagnosis and treatment of diffuse gliomas of adulthood. Nat Rev Clin Oncol 2021;18(3):170-186 (PMID 33293629) (2021) [S]</item><item>Falls and mobility from the first visit: home safety review, fall plan, physical therapy assessment once the treatment plan is set, and a check at every visit of strength in both legs, since new right-sided weakness adds to a left leg weakened by polio in childhood; watch for new weakness, fatigue or pain that could signal post-polio syndrome. Guideline: Weller M, et al. EANO guidelines on the diagnosis and treatment of diffuse gliomas of adulthood. Nat Rev Clin Oncol 2021;18(3):170-186 (PMID 33293629) (2021); Farbu E, et al. EFNS guideline on diagnosis and management of post-polio syndrome. Eur J Neurol 2006;13(8):795-801 (PMID 16879288) (2006) [S]</item><item>Distress and depression screening at each visit, plain explanations with written information, and help to keep working as long as she wishes; she decides who receives information. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Central Nervous System Cancers (2026); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression monograph (2026); Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
